# Copy this file to `.env` and paste your real key:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Only the LLM-judge sections need OPENAI_API_KEY: section 7 (the judge demo) and
# section 9 (scoring real summaries to calibrate against human ratings). Everything
# else runs offline with no key at all: the harness, the deterministic scorers, the
# echo and oracle baselines, the synthetic-failure generator, and the bootstrap.
#
# The good news: every model call is cached to artifacts/ keyed by a hash of the
# exact request, so a second run reads from disk instead of the API and is instant
# and free. You only pay for each unique (question, answer) pair once.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides (defaults shown). Keeping the judge model different from the
# system model is intentional: a model grading its own output is generous about its
# own habits, which section 9 treats as a calibration concern, not a detail.
# SYSTEM_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
# JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-4.1-nano
